The tenant onboarding flow begins with submitting the onboarding form, followed by request review in the platform admin dashboard. Next, the system provisions the tenant, creates the restaurant owner account, and sends an email invitation to the owner. Finally, the restaurant website is prepared with the necessary configurations, identity and branding and then displaying at least the initial menu and categories come from backend.


- [ ] Integrate the email delivery service (`info.nawyorders.com`).
    
- [ ] Refactor the branding endpoint to return full restaurant configuration (identity, branding, branches config, payment channels,...).
    
- [ ] Integrate the restaurant website with the menu and categories endpoints.
    
- [ ] Deploy the Restaurant Admin Panel to the VPS with authentication and staff management.
    
- [ ] Add slug input and domain selection (custom domain `restaurant_domain.com` vs. subdomain `*.nawyorders.com`) to the onboarding form.
    
- [ ] Test the full tenant provisioning flow.
